ed}| & =0 \\\\ -(1-\\lambda )+(1-\\lambda )[(2-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-1)] & =0 \\\\ -(1-\\lambda )+(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +1-1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (1-\\lambda )(\\lambda -3) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,\\,1,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416484 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184199 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e70dec8f-9828-5fe7-bdb7-47e6557fc889" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Rectangular Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4889279a-9659-5dae-8259-b1442e0b8893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416445} {:answer/id #uuid "a08ff49c-3e48-5969-9cc0-4603170a0646" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416462} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b05a8d-1f8d-58ee-8ab2-e2cf7750d0f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416464} {:answer/id #uuid "c7d2dbc4-67b2-5124-9e27-6ec2f6fd08b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416466} {:answer/id #uuid "e93e9e61-f7d3-5cb6-85a3-a9059ed558a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$9$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4889279a-9659-5dae-8259-b1442e0b8893" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416445} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd7054d7-ed2b-5613-b2fc-90c17c4791c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c791e385-b793-500d-9a77-3e468ca25a09" :question/math-academy-id "q-95359" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 8-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(8-\\lambda )-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda -5\\lambda +40-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416482 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184198 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e2bf7196-b681-5ff6-bf16-24acefa04e6c" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Singular Values of a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [